From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep reference library documents unpublished until the owner
 ticks Affiliate library.

Reference material (catalogs, installation cost sheets, price lists, spec
books) lives in cabinet_dealz.affiliate_literature with the affiliate
literature. This patch is the server half of that split. The admin page in
cabinet-frontend shows a Reference section; this is what stops those rows
reaching an affiliate.

  shared/libraryVisibility.ts
      The same file as cabinet-frontend. isAffiliateLibraryDocument now
      returns false for a reference row unless visibility is affiliate,
      isPublished is true, AND affiliateToggledAt is set. That timestamp is
      written only when the owner ticks Affiliate library. There is still no
      public state.

  affiliateResources.publishedLiterature
      Already filters with isAffiliateLibraryDocument, so the affiliate query
      enforces the rule. A category of Product Catalogs or Installation, a
      title or file name that is a catalog, cost sheet, price list, or spec
      book, or documentRole = reference, is enough. A missing documentRole
      column reads as null and the category and title rule still applies.

  affiliateLiterature.adminUpload / adminUpdate
      Accept `reference`. It writes documentRole and nothing else: it does
      not publish, and it does not clear the who/when audit. Ticking
      Affiliate library is still the only write of visibility, isPublished,
      and affiliateToggledAt / By / ByName.

  docs/sql/0273_library_reference_documents.tidb.sql
      Tom pastes this himself. It does not run from the app. Statement 3 is
      the preview. Statement 4 is the UPDATE. A second run of the ALTER
      answers "Duplicate column name 'documentRole'", which is safe to skip.

Apply from the cabinet-backend repository root:

    git apply /path/to/cabinet-backend-library-reference-documents.patch

Then paste docs/sql/0273_library_reference_documents.tidb.sql in the TiDB
editor, one line at a time. Read the preview before the UPDATE. Nothing in
this patch deploys the frontend, and nothing here is public.
---
